          body: "This is not a demand to try harder or turn over a new leaf. Birth is the one thing you cannot do for yourself — you are wholly passive to it, and it comes entirely from outside and from *above*. Jesus tells a devout, learned, powerful man that none of his devotion, learning, or power can generate the life he lacks; it has to be *given*, from God, like a second nativity. That is why Nicodemus is so disoriented: he came to add Jesus to a life he was managing well, and is told the whole self must be begotten anew. **“Water and Spirit”** (v. 5) names how — a cleansing and a new animating life, echoing Ezekiel’s promise, *“I will sprinkle clean water on you … and put a new spirit within you”* (Ezek 36:25–27). The kingdom is not seen by improvement but by rebirth.",
