          lemma: "ὑψωθῆναι … τὸν ὄφιν",
          title: "The serpent lifted up",
          body: "The image is from **Numbers 21:8–9**: bitten by snakes, Israel is healed by *looking* at a bronze serpent Moses raises on a pole — life given to all who simply look. The verb **ὑψόω**, **“lift up,”** is another Johannine two-in-one: it means both *to hoist on the cross* and *to exalt in glory* (8:28; 12:32–34). In one word Jesus names how he will heal the world — by being raised up — and the double sense insists that the cross itself is his lifting-up into glory.",
